    "long": "Monday, November 9",
    "theme": "Culture Track",
    "head": "LEARN OURS.\nBUILD YOURS.",
    "promise": "Registration at 10. Live stream at noon. Culture Code from 1.",
    "track": "A culture that runs without you.",
    "night": "Monday Mix & Mingle, the Ritz lobby bar. The hallway is the fire.",
    "featured": "Michael King",
    "featured2": "Jay Doran",
    "dhLabel": "Double Header",
    "hours": "10–6",
    "key": "He turns leadership into clarity, alignment and accountability your team can run.",
    "blurb": "Nearly 20 years leading organizations and 100-plus teams coached, then TEAMS.Coach to bring that rigor to executive teams. A repeatable method, with AI that sharpens judgment instead of replacing it. Monday he opens the Culture Track with the code your company already runs on.",
    "key2": "Culture is the system that decides whether your company outgrows you.",
    "blurb2": "Founder of Culture Matters since 2016, tying purpose, vision and values to performance and profit. Trust, judgment and accountability stay human-led. Monday afternoon he runs the Culture Cubes, two rounds where your table solves the culture puzzle live, then builds its own code to take home.",
    "head2": "THE CULTURE.\nMAN.",
    "short": "Culture",
    "evening": "Monday Night Mix & Mingle · Time to Start Making Moves · Juniper Bar · 6:30 to 9:30",
    "line": "Win by Design",
    "tab": "Monday"
   },
   {
    "date": "2026-11-10",
    "label": "Tue",
    "long": "Tuesday, November 10",
    "theme": "Growth Track",
    "head": "WE GROW.\nTHEN THE LOUNGE.",
    "promise": "Close more. Come back stronger.",
    "track": "Built to close, beside Built to Sell.",
    "night": "The Liquidity Lounge, 6:30 PM. Cocktail attire.",
    "featured": "Tim Storey",
    "featured2": "Richard C. Wilson",
    "dhLabel": "Double Header",
    "_note": "MDC said \"Monday\" for Storey + Wilson; both speak Tuesday, placed Tuesday [ASSUMPTION]",
    "hours": "8–6",
    "key": "He builds platforms that carry a mission beyond any one founder.",
    "blurb": "From Compton, where he lost his father and his brother young, to one of the most sought-after comeback coaches alive. Author of The Miracle Mentality and Comeback & Beyond, he has walked some of the best-known names in entertainment, sports and business out of their setbacks and back into their calling. Through Lead With Love, Miracle Mentality and Real Storey's he is building an organization that scales without depending on him. Tuesday he delivers the featured keynote at noon, then hosts the Liquidity Lounge that night.",
    "key2": "Nineteen years inside family office deals, boiled down to ten insights.",
    "blurb2": "Founder of Family Office Club, the network connecting ultra-wealthy families, their advisors and the founders who raise capital from them. Nineteen years inside the deals, watching a billion dollars of transactions close, and a clear read on what the families actually want from a founder. Tuesday he brings his top ten family office insights to the room: how capital decides, what kills a deal, and how a CEO gets invited back. If your exit needs a buyer with patience and a long memory, this is the hour.",
    "head2": "THE FAMILY OFFICE KEYNOTE.",
    "short": "Growth",
    "evening": "Ladies' Night at the Liquidity Lounge · Cocktail Attire · The Conservatory · 6:30 to 9:30",
    "line": "Grow by Design",
    "tab": "Tuesday"
   },
   {
    "date": "2026-11-11",
    "label": "Wed",
    "long": "Wednesday, November 11",
    "theme": "ExitTrack",
    "head": "THE EXIT TRACK.\nWHY YOU COME.",
    "promise": "I built the track. He drives it. You ride.",
    "track": "The track itself.",
    "night": "A night out together.",
    "featured": "Roland Frasier",
    "featured2": "Shawn French",
    "track2": "The Double Header",
    "head2": "THE EXIT KEYNOTE.",
    "dhLabel": "Double Header",
    "hours": "8–6",
    "key": "Advisor on 1,000-plus deals. He drives the Exit Track.",
    "blurb": "Part of exits to KKR, SoftBank and a Blackstone company, after 14 years practicing law for founders. Co-founder of DigitalMarketer and Scalable, host of the Business Lunch podcast, and an advisor on more than a thousand deals. He leads the 36-month Exit Track that moves a CEO from owning a job to owning an asset: the M.A.S.T.E.R. mind, the track, and why it exists. Wednesday is his day.",
    "key2": "The Determined Society host on what discipline cost him and taught him.",
    "blurb2": "Built The Determined Society into a platform with millions of listens by asking the hard questions of top names in entertainment, sports and business. LSU baseball, a corporate sales career, and now he answers those questions himself. Wednesday he gives the Exit Keynote, then sits for the Spotlight Podcast double header with Advisor Tim Storey: two parts, two chairs, the questions he usually asks turned on him.",
    "short": "ExitTrack",
    "evening": "Chairman-Led Member-to-Member Dinners · Explore the Ritz & Restaurants · 6:30 to 9:30",
    "line": "Exit by Design",
    "tab": "Wednesday"
   },
   {
    "date": "2026-11-12",
    "label": "Thu",
    "long": "Thursday, November 12",
    "theme": "Advisory Track",
    "head": "BUILT TO RUN WITHOUT YOU.",
    "promise": "Seven phases every business passes through, and the pinch point holding yours.",
    "track": "Freedom from founder dependency.",
    "night": "Member Dinners.",
    "featured": "Ian Taylor",
    "featured2": "Carl Gould",
    "dhLabel": "Double Header",
    "hours": "8–6",
    "key": "He rewires the identity and decision patterns that cap your performance.",
    "blurb": "Chief Human Performance Architect embedded with leading NYC fintech firms. His Human Operating System framework and ARISE Method have been used with hundreds of clients, from children to senior executives. Thursday's keynote, The Price of Becoming, is the identity work behind the exit.",
    "key2": "He finds the pinch point holding your business at its current phase.",
    "blurb2": "Maps every business through seven phases, from Strategic Planning to Succession, and shows owners which pinch point blocks the next one. His first company doubled every year for seven years. Thursday's workshop, Freedom From Founder Dependency, is the plan to run without you.",
    "head2": "SEVEN STAGES.\nONE PINCH POINT.",
